<title>UK: Shell says still losing 100 kbpd Nigerian output.</title>
<headline>Shell says still losing 100 kbpd Nigerian output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell said on Tuesday it was still losing 100,000 barrels per day (bpd) of Nigerian crude oil production after Niger Delta villagers occupied six flow stations on Saturday.</p>
<p>But exports and other supply commitments continued to be met, a Shell spokesman in London said.</p>
</text>
